  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rhino &amp; Tiger Conservation Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;This project will gather information about the illegal trade of rhino horn in Vietnam by engaging and training Vietnamese government law enforcement agencies and increasing awareness about the plight of rhinos and the harm done by the rhino horn trade in the local media. .Specific activities will include (1) a study of the illegal trade dynamics in Vietnam, specifically rhino horn consumption and domestic demand; (2) conduct two workshops for a total of 100 government officers from the judiciary, including court authorities, prosecutors office and peoples committees in Ho Chi Minh City and Hanoi, to.increase understanding of illegal rhino horn trade and relevant laws and treaties; (3) conduct one journalist training workshop in Hanoi for 25 local journalists to provide information on the international wildlife trade (specifically rhino horn), guidance on key issues and messaging; and (4) provide technical assistance and support to the CITES MA and other relevant national agencies on management of their rhino horn and elephant ivory stockpile..&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
